# Vercel upload filter.
#
# Explicit rather than relying on .gitignore: without this file the CLI uploaded
# 167MB, pulling in the 120MB source asset tree and the locally built dist/ on
# top of the 23MB the site actually needs.
#
# Two rules matter:
#   - assets/ is excluded. It is a macOS-only input tree (prepare-assets.sh needs
#     sips + cwebp, which have no Linux build) and must never be processed on
#     Vercel's builders.
#   - dist/ is excluded. Vercel runs the build itself from source; shipping our
#     local output as well just doubles the upload.
#
# public/ is deliberately NOT excluded. public/assets/ holds the optimised FBX
# meshes, the PBR maps and the intro sting — the pipeline cannot regenerate them
# in CI, so this committed copy is the only one that reaches the deployment.
# Ignoring it produces a build that succeeds and then loads no 3D at all.

assets/
dist/
.vercel/output/
node_modules/

.git/
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Agent tooling, not part of the project
.agents/
skills-lock.json
